Local skills live here, and they WIN collisions against published ones.

Skills resolve first-found-wins, and this directory sits above plugin skills in the
chain. A file here with the same name as a published skill shadows it silently: no
warning, no error, nothing in any log.

That is not necessarily wrong. Under an innersource model, overriding a standard is how
you signal that the standard is wrong. Open an issue against the source plugin so the
fix reaches everyone.

This is also the middle stage of the contribution path. A folder here containing
.claude-plugin/plugin.json loads as <name>@skills-dir on the next session, with no
marketplace and no install step.
